# Focused verification lane

Use [afenda-focused-verification](../skills/afenda-focused-verification/SKILL.md) for test/check selection after code edits, failures, timeouts, or architecture/register changes.

## Binding rule

- Use the smallest reliable check set that covers the changed surface.
- Prefer package-local `lint`, `typecheck`, and `test` commands.
- Add consumers only when package exports, contracts, schemas, or app actions changed.
- Run `pnpm validate:modules` when module manifests/registers/permissions/queries/commands/events/table ownership changed.
- Do not retry root-wide commands after timeout/failure as an edit-loop tactic.
- Treat `pnpm test`, `pnpm check`, `pnpm build:check`, and broad `turbo run lint typecheck test build` as final CI-parity gates only.

## Hook

`beforeShellExecution` -> `.cursor/hooks/focused-verification-lane.mjs` asks before broad root verification commands unless `AFENDA_ALLOW_BROAD_VERIFY=1` is present in the environment or command.

Do not rename, split, or wrap commands to bypass the hook. If a broad gate is required, state why and ask the user before running it.
